From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:13:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 18/23] MSL: transform feedback capture for MoltenVK's compute
 capture stage

- Only the capture_output_to_buffer version of a vertex shader captures; the
  rasterizing vertex function ignores the Xfb decorations (outputs are no longer
  redirected to the capture locals there).
- The capture writes a primitive to every buffer or none: the count that fits
  in every buffer (from the offset and size in MoltenVK's capture state) is
  written, and thread 0 records written/needed primitives and bytes per buffer
  for a following dispatch that advances the offsets.
- Captured outputs are thread-local, so component writes don't take the device
  pointer cast.
- gl_VertexIndex, gl_InstanceIndex, gl_BaseVertex and gl_BaseInstance in vertex
  kernels include the stage-in grid origin (first vertex / vertex offset and
  first instance).
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 208 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 spirv_msl.hpp |   4 +-
 2 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 110 deletions(-)

